{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1141930-a-sphere-of-light","id":1141930,"title":"A Sphere of Light","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-09-19T16:24:23-07:00","id":1141930,"title":"A Sphere of Light","content":"I have seen the cWoD/nWoD/CoD and their dark themes running pretty grimdark on the grim/noble scale of fantasy or whatever. What would a place of all good things (a plane of light, Heaven, Nirvana, you know all good places) would look like to the inhabitants of the Fallen World and its peripheral realities steeped in darkness and horror? For its horror, the Sphere is joy, for its fear, the place would actually have <i>hope</i>. What do y'all think?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7106-extant-reality","name":"Extant Reality","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7106_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"155"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-19T18:18:52-07:00","id":1141965,"title":"","content":"I know the Underworld has a few heaven realms, and it used to have a Valhalla.<br /> <br /> Far as I'm aware vampires don't actually get a happy ending, so I imagine that such a place could potentially burn them to ashes.<br /> <br /> I think the closest thing to a heaven realm other than Underworld realms would be the Supernal Realm from mage the awakening, specifically the Aether.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12436-ever-professional","name":"Ever Professional","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12436_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"506"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-19T18:26:14-07:00","id":1141970,"title":"","content":"It might be going against what you intended, but the first thing i thought of was a lower depth with ''darkness' being whats missing. With a member of that realm being absolutely fascinated by concepts like evil, hatred or despair. Apologies that this is probably the very opposite of what you meant.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Completed campaign: Scion 2nd Edition. Les L\u00e9gendes Currently playing: Being a dad for a 3 year old daughter and a 2 years old son and now a beautiful new baby.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11312-maitrecorbo","name":"Maitrecorbo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11312_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"719"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-20T00:35:53-07:00","id":1142061,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ever Professional</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1141930-a-sphere-of-light?p=1141965#post1141965\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I know the Underworld has a few heaven realms, and it used to have a Valhalla.<br /> <br /> Far as I'm aware vampires don't actually get a happy ending, so I imagine that such a place could potentially burn them to ashes.<br /> <br /> I think the closest thing to a heaven realm other than Underworld realms would be the Supernal Realm from mage the awakening, specifically the Aether.</div> </div> </div> </div>I wouldn't say the Aether is any kind of heaven equivalent. Without the grounding force of the Watchtower the Aether is a chaotic maelstrom of clashing energy and forces. It has light, sure, but it's the blinding light of a supernova rather than any sort of warm light of salvation. Not to mention that raw exposure to the 'place' kills you deader than just about anything else in the entire setting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2309-ashenrogue","name":"Ashenrogue","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1388"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-20T00:58:47-07:00","id":1142065,"title":"","content":"I think it overlooks the reasons for the CofD world being so dark. One of the things I personally like about it over most such settings is that the books actually do go into why the world is as it is, or at least imply reasons, it's not just abstractly awful.<br /> <br /> You might as well ask what such a place would look like to us in the real world; people tend to struggle to articulate Heaven in a satisfying way.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-20T01:48:24-07:00","id":1142074,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ashenrogue</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1141930-a-sphere-of-light?p=1142061#post1142061\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I wouldn't say the Aether is any kind of heaven equivalent. Without the grounding force of the Watchtower the Aether is a chaotic maelstrom of clashing energy and forces. It has light, sure, but it's the blinding light of a supernova rather than any sort of warm light of salvation. Not to mention that raw exposure to the 'place' kills you deader than just about anything else in the entire setting.</div> </div> </div> </div><i>Tome of the Watchtowers</i> specifically mentions the theme of Obrimos to be &quot;hope&quot;, so Aether is at least in part a &quot;heaven&quot; as people commonly understand it. It's a judgmental place and you need to learn how to wield the Power properly, but it still is a heaven.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5973-prometheus","name":"Prometheus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5973_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-20T01:52:38-07:00","id":1142075,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prometheus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1141930-a-sphere-of-light?p=1142074#post1142074\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><i>Tome of the Watchtowers</i> specifically mentions the theme of Obrimos to be &quot;hope&quot;, so Aether is at least in part a &quot;heaven&quot; as people commonly understand it. It's a judgmental place and you need to learn how to wield the Power properly, but it still is a heaven.</div> </div> </div> </div>To me it is more hope in the energetic potential of the universe and that it won't end with the heat death of it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","name":"Malus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1562"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-20T02:14:48-07:00","id":1142076,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Malus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1141930-a-sphere-of-light?p=1142075#post1142075\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> To me it is more hope in the energetic potential of the universe and that it won't end with the heat death of it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Look in detail at the &quot;Mood: Hope&quot; part and &quot;Character Concepts&quot; part of the chapter, they speak for themselves. Sure, Obrimos are about power, but they are <i>also</i> about the light of hope. One doesn't exclude the other.<br /> <br /> Also, to correct my previous statement, their Theme is actually Strength, it's their Mood that is hope, but that's just a technicality.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5973-prometheus","name":"Prometheus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5973_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-20T03:03:15-07:00","id":1142082,"title":"","content":"In my opinion, hope is a very important theme for any good horror story.<br /> <br /> After all, hope is exactly what you feel the moment you think you managed to escape the slasher's murder house, just a moment before they stab you in the face.<br /> <br /> In a more serious not, hope is important just because it gives the characters a motivation to keep struggling. If everyone knows that the monster would win and that they have no way out, they won't put much of a struggle. Hope makes them think that there is a chance for a victory, that there is a chance to make the world into less dark and more illuminated. And things like Heaven of some kind do support that fragile, distant hope.<br /> <br /> However, it is still an horror story, and even hope should be tainted with blood. While things like the Empyrean may exist in the setting, there is much closer Heaven than those distant realms, and Heaven which is actually quit achievable, if you are willing to make the needed sacrifices. I mean, look at some of the Infrastructures presented in the GMC- some of them actually have pretty good consequences, giving those who live in their boundaries high life quality and safe place to live in, a place where they are safe from the horrors of the world and the darkness which waits to devour them. The only thing they need to do is making a human sacrifice or two once a month, that's it. You may even choose the ones to kill- for Heaven doesn't distinguish blood from blood, and punishing the wicked is part of Heaven's job, too. Heaven on earth is possible- but the price in blood must still be paid.<br /> <br /> There is hope in the CofD- there always is. But you to open Pandora's Box if you wish to get it out.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-20T03:17:35-07:00","id":1142083,"title":"","content":"I think you could get a lot of mileage out of the &quot;Lower Depth missing a negative thing&quot; idea.<br /> <br /> There'd probably be some sort of twist that makes it a horrific faux-utopia, obviously.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-20T05:52:19-07:00","id":1142110,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Maitrecorbo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1141930-a-sphere-of-light?p=1141970#post1141970\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It might be going against what you intended, but the first thing i thought of was a lower depth with ''darkness' being whats missing. With a member of that realm being absolutely fascinated by concepts like evil, hatred or despair. Apologies that this is probably the very opposite of what you meant.</div> </div> </div> </div>Actually, I believe there is one. There is a lower depth that the Strix can go to when they are at ten shadow potency, and other younger strix will be able to leave said realm.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12436-ever-professional","name":"Ever Professional","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12436_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"506"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-20T06:31:48-07:00","id":1142118,"title":"","content":"IIRC it's generally accepted that the Strix realm lacks Life.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-20T07:01:39-07:00","id":1142124,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1141930-a-sphere-of-light?p=1142118#post1142118\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">IIRC it's generally accepted that the Strix realm lacks Life.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ah, right. I mostly know requiem lore, so I don't often think about the lower depths (vampire for the most part not supporting/leading to that kind of play).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12436-ever-professional","name":"Ever Professional","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12436_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"506"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-20T07:09:57-07:00","id":1142129,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prometheus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1141930-a-sphere-of-light?p=1142074#post1142074\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><i>Tome of the Watchtowers</i> specifically mentions the theme of Obrimos to be &quot;hope&quot;, so Aether is at least in part a &quot;heaven&quot; as people commonly understand it. It's a judgmental place and you need to learn how to wield the Power properly, but it still is a heaven.</div> </div> </div> </div>The nature of the supernal realms has been tweaked and expounded on pretty heavily since Tome of the Watchtowers, and from what we know about it now it is in no way any sort of heaven; not for anything that isn't already pure supernal truth.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2309-ashenrogue","name":"Ashenrogue","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1388"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-20T07:30:47-07:00","id":1142139,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ashenrogue</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1141930-a-sphere-of-light?p=1142129#post1142129\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The nature of the supernal realms has been tweaked and expounded on pretty heavily since Tome of the Watchtowers, and from what we know about it now it is in no way any sort of heaven; not for anything that isn't already pure supernal truth.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, I haven't seen the idea outright repudiated anywhere, so I presume that, like other things from 1E not outright contradicted by new lore, the idea is still valid. And of course it's not a heaven for anything not Supernal, as everything not Supernal gets burned to dust if it tries to enter. It's more about the ideas the realm represents in the Phenomenal World. Regardless, Obrimos are still mentioned in 2E as holding culture heroes bringing enlightenment and civilization to Sleepers in reverence, so not much appears to have changed. And Dave also described Obrimos as the least changed Path with the most changed Arcana in the relevant dev blog.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5973-prometheus","name":"Prometheus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5973_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-20T16:28:52-07:00","id":1142333,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1141930-a-sphere-of-light?p=1142118#post1142118\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">IIRC it's generally accepted that the Strix realm lacks Life.</div> </div> </div> </div>It lacks Vitae, wich I think is a significant distinction.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-20T17:24:19-07:00","id":1142351,"title":"","content":"It's significant in that it goes from making sense to <i>not </i>making sense. Vitae is just how strix and vampires store the life they suck out of people. It doesn't exist <i>without </i>them. How can that be the concept that their realm lacks?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-20T21:09:11-07:00","id":1142407,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1141930-a-sphere-of-light?p=1142351#post1142351\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's significant in that it goes from making sense to <i>not </i>making sense. Vitae is just how strix and vampires store the life they suck out of people. It doesn't exist <i>without </i>them. How can that be the concept that their realm lacks?</div> </div> </div> </div>It's the thing that they take out of the world. If the vital essence vampires drain from people was just Life then there would be absolutely zero reason for soulless people to have no Vitae to drain.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-21T02:38:40-07:00","id":1142441,"title":"","content":"AFAIK that only presents a problem when Breath Drinking. So, really it seems more like the soul is a conduit for life taken in the form of health points than the actual source there. <br /> <br /> But yeah, I suppose the thing they crave is a little more rarefied that Life in general, being found in spirits and other stuff. I wouldn't call it vitae though. That's just the form that energy takes once they harvest it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-21T07:58:52-07:00","id":1142511,"title":"","content":"They don't really take it out of the world, anyways, any more than humans take proteins and carbohydrates and oxygen out. While the strix can create portals to their home world at the rare top end of their power set, most strix are natives of Earth.<br /> <br /> Regarding the origin of the strix, p200. 'That\u2019s a long, long time ago; and contrary to popular myth among the Kindred, the Strix have never gone away. They may have broken into this world from another in the primeval nights, but none remember it, or are believable when they claim to. The Strix don\u2019t age, but they do die when destroyed or when they reproduce, and all Owls encountered in the moderns nights are as native to the World of Darkness as the Kindred are.'<br /> <br /> At the risk of being silly, is humans taking 'food' out a thing? Prometheans can subsist on rocks and paper. Werewolves eat raw meat and spirits. Vampires drink blood. The more human you remain the more you hunger for the major food groups, also the minor food groups.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 09-21-2017, 11:22 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-21T08:41:37-07:00","id":1142536,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1141930-a-sphere-of-light?p=1142511#post1142511\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">At the risk of being silly, is humans taking 'food' out a thing?</div> </div> </div> </div>Vampires and the Strix don't turn Vitae <i>into</i> anything, is where this falls flat \u2014 it's fuel for restoring their unhealing bodies and using their occult abilities, but the nearest thing we have to a regular vampiric ecology is &quot;vampires messing with stuff sometimes makes it more likely to lead to more vampires.&quot;<br /> <br /> If humans had a one-stop digestive system then yes, that would definitely be taking food out of a thing; we're talking about a magical predator-parasite that corrupts the living to better sustain itself, not a biologically mundane animal that breathes and sheds and bleeds. Vampirism is a wound.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-21T08:46:28-07:00","id":1142538,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1141930-a-sphere-of-light?p=1142536#post1142536\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Vampires and the Strix don't turn Vitae <i>into</i> anything, is where this falls flat \u2014 it's fuel for restoring their unhealing bodies and using their occult abilities, but the nearest thing we have to a regular vampiric ecology is &quot;vampires messing with stuff sometimes makes it more likely to lead to more vampires.&quot;[<br /> <br /> If humans had a one-stop digestive system then yes, that would definitely be taking food out of a thing; we're talking about a magical predator-parasite that corrupts the living to better sustain itself, not a biologically mundane animal that breathes and sheds and bleeds. Vampirism is a wound.</div> </div> </div> </div>So they're more similar to robots than humans from an energy-to-ecology perspective.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}